<title>SWEDEN: Ericsson signs GSM contract in Slovakia.</title>
<headline>Ericsson signs GSM contract in Slovakia.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish telecoms group LM AB Ericsson said on Tuesday that it had signed a GSM contract with Eurotel, owned by the Slovak PTT, U.S. West and Bell Atlantic Corp.  </p>
<p>Ericsson said the contract was its first order for public telecommunications in Slovakia and included new switches and radio base station equipment.</p>
<p>&quot;Commercial service will begin in February 1997 and a very fast roll-out of the network is planned,&quot; Ericsson said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Belinda Goldsmith, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1045</p>
</text>
